  "repairs": [
    "Link diagnostics now separate retirement (including any non-presentation mutation), element identity, base, signature, navigation kind/fragment identity, layout and label/destination metadata.",
    "Pointer-selected new-context links with unchanged document-navigation capability can survive class/style-only retirement. The app opens the retained URL using native navigation without activating page handlers. Exact original element, base, signature, URL, label, navigation kind, geometry, hit point, native source/owner/control and login gates still apply.",
    "Ordinary link activation, Enter/key activation and fragment actions retain strict retirement. Non-presentation mutation and change-then-restoration remain rejected.",
    "The private retirement classification was renamed from editingRetired to nonPresentationRetired because native editing and document navigation now use the same distinction. Existing typing behavior and full-page terminal validation remain unchanged."
  ],
